course: dictionary
lesson: 13361
title: Hardback and paperback
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hardback is a word you will meet in libraries and bookshops. It can be a noun, a thing: «The story came out in hardback.» Here a hardback is a book with a stiff, strong cover.
explain: Hardback can also be an adjective, a word that describes a thing: «She read a hardback book about dinosaurs.» The word hardback tells you what kind of book it is, so it describes the book.
explain: Context gives you the clues. When a sentence mentions shelves, covers, or a price, check whether the word is naming the book or describing it. Then swap in your meaning: «a book with a stiff, strong cover» should still make sense.
fact: Hardback means a book with a stiff, strong cover.
fact: Hardback can be a noun («a hardback») or an adjective («a hardback book»).
fact: The phrase «in hardback» means the book is printed with a stiff cover.
fact: Hardbacks last longer, but they cost more and weigh more than paperbacks.
fact: A paperback is the other kind of book, with a softer cover.
exercise: In «The story came out in hardback», what does hardback mean? | A bag for carrying books | *A book with a stiff, strong cover | A quiet corner of a library | A story told out loud
exercise: In «She read a hardback book about dinosaurs», which word describes the book? | She | about | *hardback | dinosaurs
exercise: Why might a child choose a paperback instead of a hardback? | It is always bigger | It has a stiffer cover | *It costs less and weighs less | It lasts longer
test: «The library has a new hardback edition of the atlas.» What does hardback mean here? | *A book with a stiff, strong cover | A type of library shelf | A map that folds up | A page with no words
test: Which is true? Hardbacks cost more and weigh more than paperbacks. | Hardbacks are always cheaper | Paperbacks have stiff covers | Hardbacks are never found in libraries | *Hardbacks usually cost more and weigh more
exam: Tom carried the heavy hardback home from the shop. What is hardback doing in this sentence? | It means a heavy bag | It describes the book, as an adjective | *It names the book, as a noun, meaning a book with a stiff, strong cover | It is the name of the shop
